WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/FrontendErrorsCard.tsx — the last-hour rolling summary of
  browser-reported frontend errors (the data that backed the deleted /admin "Frontend Errors" panel).
  Hook: useWebErrorsSummary() → GET /admin/web-errors/summary → WebErrorsSummary { total, top:
  [{ name, route, count }], window_seconds, as_of } (types/admin.ts). Render branches:
    isLoading                 → two <Skeleton h-6/> bars.
    !data                     → "Unable to load frontend error summary." (muted).
    data                      → panel: Bug glyph + "Frontend errors (last hour)" (uppercase, muted);
                                fmtInt(total ?? 0) [2xl tabular] + "reported by browser sessions";
                                top.length > 0 ? <ul> rows [ <Badge neutral>{name || '—'}</Badge> ·
                                  mono cyan route {route || '—'} · right fmtInt(count ?? 0) ]
                                : "No frontend errors reported in the last hour."
  Helpers (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
    fmtInt(v) = fmtNumber(v, 0) = safeNumber(v).toLocaleString(locale, { min:0, max:0 }); safeNumber
    coerces non-finite ⇒ 0. name/route `|| '—'` falls back to the em dash on an empty string.
  i18n  : the web source is "anonymous" — hardcoded English literals (no t() calls). Per the native
          no-English-literals rule every literal is promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "FrontendErrorsCard").

